<title>USA: LUCENT TO TAKE AFTER-TAX CHARGE $950 MLN - WSJ.</title>
<headline>LUCENT TO TAKE AFTER-TAX CHARGE $950 MLN - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lucent Technologies Inc will take an after-tax charge of $950 million, or $1.47 per share, related to its $1.8 billion acquisition of Octel Communications, the Wall Street Journal reported.</p>
<p>The charge, to be taken in the company's fourth quarter ended September 30, will likely result in a quarterly loss, the paper said in its electronic edition.</p>
<p>The company disclosed the charge in a regulatory filing Wednesday, the paper said.</p>
<p>Analysts had expected the company to post a profit of $0.51 per share for the quarter, according to a First Call survey.</p>
<p>Lucent shares fell 14/16 Wednesday to 82-9/16.</p>
